  "bodyTypst": "#image(\"/imgs/ap-calc-ab-2019-frq-03-diagram-01.png\", width: 65%)\n\nThe continuous function $f$ is defined on the closed interval $- 6 <= x <= 5$. The figure above shows a portion of the graph of $f$, consisting of two line segments and a quarter of a circle centered at the point (5, 3). It is known that the point $(3 \\,3 - sqrt(5))$ is on the graph of $f$.\n\n(a) If $integral_(- 6)^(5) f(x) d x = 7$, find the value of $integral_(- 6)^(- 2) f(x) d x$. Show the work that leads to your answer.\n\n(b) Evaluate $integral_(3)^(5)lr((2 f'(x)+ 4)) d x$.\n\n(c) The function $g$ is given by $g(x)= integral_(- 2)^(x) f(t) d t$. Find the absolute maximum value of $g$ on the interval $- 2 <= x <= 5$. Justify your answer.\n\n(d) Find $lim_(x -> 1) frac(10^(x)- 3 f'(x),f(x)- arctan x)$.",
